                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "The game goes SUPER slow for the first level, which makes it very boring up front. While this works well for the fact there are no controls/instructions provided, it would be better to have that instead. Getting a 100% perfect run is easy on the first level. The second level, well, it's obliteratingly hard. If the difficulty scaled better, this would be more enjoyable. As it is, I was lulled into complacency only to be wiped out a few minutes later. A second try resulted in the same thing.\n\nMoreover, there are bugs abound. First, I pressed a few different key combinations trying to figure out how to play. I managed to turn on (I presume unintentional) perma-autofire. With the keybinding being what it is, this was actually a nice thing to work with. Alas, I couldn't figure out how to turn it on or off during subsequent plays.\n\nNext, when I died (I only died in the second level, at the same point, so not sure if it's specific to that, or in general), the game kept playing! I lost all my lives, my ship disappeared, but the enemies kept coming and kept shooting! I had to force quit the game to get back to the menu.\n\nThird, the achievements don't work. As I said, I made it to level 2, which should have earned me the \"[i]Space Fighter -- Finish Level 01 - Star Chase[/i]\" achievement, but... nope.\n\nLastly, some menu elements on the start screen overlap if you don't set your resolution properly.\n\n\nThat being said, this shooter game wasn't terrible, more just frustrating and it felt incomplete. In its current state, I do not recommend.",
